# Task 2 - Area estimation with Monte Carlo Simulation

In this task, we will utilize Monte Carlo simulation to estimate the area enclosed by a curve defined in polar coordinates. The curve is given by the function:

$$
r(t) = \exp(\cos(t)) - 2 \cdot \cos(4 \cdot t) - \sin\left(\frac{t}{12}\right)^5, \quad t \in [-\pi, \pi]
$$

We will use polar to Cartesian conversion to translate the polar coordinates 
$$
x = r(t) \cdot \cos(t)
$$

$$
y = r(t) \cdot \sin(t)
$$

### 2.1 Visualise the function and the area

In this task, we will explore the area enclosed by a polar curve and estimate its area using Monte Carlo simulation.The objective is to visualize the area enclosed by the curve in the Cartesian plane, and use Monte Carlo simulation to estimate the area within the curve.
``` {r task2.1}
r_function <- function(t) {
  tryCatch({
    exp(cos(t)) - 2 * cos(4 * t) - sin(t / 12)^5
  }, error = function(e) {
    stop("Error in r_function: ", e$message)
  })
}

polar_to_cartesian <- function(t) {
  tryCatch({
    r <- r_function(t)
    c(r * cos(t), r * sin(t))
  }, error = function(e) {
    stop("Error in polar_to_cartesian: ", e$message)
  })
}

monte_carlo_area <- function(n_samples) {
  if (!is.numeric(n_samples) || n_samples <= 0) {
    stop("Error: n_samples must be a positive integer.")
  }

  t_samples <- tryCatch({
    runif(n_samples, -pi, pi)
  }, error = function(e) {
    stop("Error generating t_samples: ", e$message)
  })
  
  points <- tryCatch({
    t(sapply(t_samples, polar_to_cartesian))
  }, error = function(e) {
    stop("Error in converting polar to Cartesian: ", e$message)
  })
  
  x_min <- min(points[, 1])
  x_max <- max(points[, 1])
  y_min <- min(points[, 2])
  y_max <- max(points[, 2])

  random_points <- tryCatch({
    cbind(runif(n_samples, x_min, x_max), runif(n_samples, y_min, y_max))
  }, error = function(e) {
    stop("Error generating random_points: ", e$message)
  })

  inside_area <- tryCatch({
    sum(apply(random_points, 1, function(p) {
      sqrt(p[1]^2 + p[2]^2) <= max(sapply(t_samples, r_function))
    }))
  }, error = function(e) {
    stop("Error calculating inside_area: ", e$message)
  })
  
  area_estimate <- (inside_area / n_samples) * (x_max - x_min) * (y_max - y_min)
  return(area_estimate)
}

t_vals <- seq(-pi, pi, length.out = 1000)
polar_coords <- tryCatch({
  t(sapply(t_vals, polar_to_cartesian))
}, error = function(e) {
  stop("Error in converting polar to Cartesian: ", e$message)
})

x_vals <- polar_coords[, 1]
y_vals <- polar_coords[, 2]

ggplot() +
  geom_path(aes(x = x_vals, y = y_vals), color = "blue", size = 1) +
  coord_fixed() +
  theme_minimal() +
  labs(title = "Polar Curve and Enclosed Area", x = "X", y = "Y")

n_samples <- 100
estimated_area <- tryCatch({
  monte_carlo_area(n_samples)
}, error = function(e) {
  stop("Error estimating area: ", e$message)
})

cat("Estimated Area Enclosed by the Curve:", estimated_area, "\n")
```
